  "summary": "Emmy Noether, born in Erlangen in 1882, became a leading mathematician in abstract algebra. Invited to Göttingen in 1915, she was granted habilitation there in 1919. She was dismissed in April 1933 for being Jewish, moved to Bryn Mawr College, and died there in 1935.",
